  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_e45a60a3d172438680f4efe3e7cc7b34",
      "statement": "handleAuthRevokeAll regenerates and persists both cfg.Token and cfg.AuthCookieSecret together, which simultaneously invalidates the token URL, the token cookie, and every PIN-session cookie at once, including for the device that issued the revoke-all request itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/auth_handlers.go#L72-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89f8ef1d3e445517b9ff213d938d0c74f4bb6de3004a09ecf999d840236ee02d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6fcc6232328448e8a979e9c84a7b5254",
      "statement": "If persisting the new token/secret to disk fails after handleAuthRevokeAll has already updated them in memory, the handler explicitly rolls the in-memory config back to the previous token and secret before returning an error, rather than leaving new in-memory credentials that were never written to disk or returned to any caller, which would otherwise cut off all external Hub access until a process restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/auth_handlers.go#L101-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:46a08f2b7a15be249a25006d6fa1d400b10b38eb529d50c58a75adeb7bd3ffb8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5b36a0d057564a3ebcc7672e8d23a6dc",
      "statement": "handleAuthRevokeAll requires a remote (non-loopback) caller to already hold a valid PIN cookie before the revoke-all action is allowed, specifically because remotePINRequired() normally lets a bootstrap caller through when no PIN is configured yet, and without this extra gate any remote holder of the current token could rotate the token/cookie secret and lock the legitimate owner out first.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/auth_handlers.go#L76-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e4ff31782e731ea019b5087e7a9a7b191d2be76ed6f003939fb326225d7b7dcf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_840a9049d53044f9891d5f38ca9acd31",
      "statement": "POST /api/auth/logout clears only the calling browser's own token/pin cookies without rotating the shared token or cookie secret, and is authorized through guardBase (token+method+Host+Origin) without the PIN gate, on the reasoning that possessing a valid cookie already proves the caller may end that session while a request with no cookie has nothing to log out, closing off both a CSRF path and a force-logout-someone-else path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/auth_handlers.go#L20-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ecdb4c7d58011cf14f2c148187d61a5d4285a9507e490f3dfcdc849898d1dbcd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2f78d8dedcd2489488b3577922aa9a17",
      "statement": "cfg.RemotePINHash is bcrypt-hashed and off by default; when set, a successful PIN login issues a signed expiring cookie (HMAC-SHA256 over AuthCookieSecret, payload expiry.nonce.deviceHash) rather than treating the PIN as a per-request bearer credential, the cookie is honored only when its nonce is in the server-side session registry and its device hash matches the requesting device, and it is invalidated wholesale by the same AuthCookieSecret rotation that revoke-all performs on the token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/hub/auth_handlers.go#L64-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:316ae5c94c10d72da1f7b5a278d10383a81e954593c08be1b4556f7e2e8c3e5c:"
