    {
      "id": "claim_791b856214d0471e8c2483bee06bef0b",
      "statement": "HTTPS tailscale serve is preferred over a bare tailnet IP because a plain-HTTP origin on a raw IP loses secure-context status in the browser, disabling the service worker, Web Push, PWA installation, and microphone access; an SSH local-forward to http://127.0.0.1:<port> is kept as the one remaining plain-HTTP path that still qualifies as a secure context.",
