    {
      "id": "claim_de3112bb5ee14be5a1a60302811168e5",
      "statement": "A first logically-remote connection from a device not previously seen (identified by a truncated SHA-256 of the remote IP, or the Tailscale-User-Login identity behind tailscale serve, plus a coarse browser/OS bucket of the User-Agent, never the raw values) triggers a new-device notification through the existing push/ntfy/webhook channels regardless of the user's configured notify.events filter, checked on the index page, on a WebSocket UI attach, and on a successful PIN login; a previously-seen device is not re-notified on every reconnect, bounded by a 24-hour TTL and a soft cap of 256 tracked devices.",
